---
/**
 * Credit and recommendation for Jessica Talisman's Ontology Pipeline, the reference the knowledge
 * graph pages are built around.
 */
---
<aside class="book-credit" aria-labelledby="book-credit-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">The best resource on this</p>
  <h2 id="book-credit-heading"><a href="https://technicspub.com/ontology-pipeline/" rel="noopener"><cite>Ontology Pipeline: A Framework for Knowledge Engineering</cite></a></h2>
  <p class="byline">Jessica Talisman · Technics Publications</p>
  <p>
    How to get from a list of terms to a knowledge graph worth having: controlled vocabulary, metadata
    standards, taxonomy, thesaurus, ontology, then the graph, each stage preparing the next. Talisman draws
    on librarians' practice and the ANSI/NISO Z39.19 standard, and the book is the clearest account we know
    of what a knowledge graph needs before any database is chosen. Our knowledge graph pages lean on its
    architecture throughout; the book goes much further.
  </p>
  <ul class="links">
    <li><a href="https://technicspub.com/ontology-pipeline/" rel="noopener">Get the book</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://jessicatalisman.substack.com/" rel="noopener">Intentional Arrangement</a>, her Substack</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.ontologypipeline.com/" rel="noopener">ontologypipeline.com</a></li>
  </ul>
</aside>

<style>
  .book-credit {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; max-width: 90ch;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-brand-accent);
    border-radius: 6px; background: var(--color-surface);
  }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0; font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--color-text-tertiary); }
  h2 { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.3; }
  h2 a { color: var(--color-text); }
  .byline { margin: 0.2rem 0 0.6rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  p { line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem; margin: 0.6rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .links a { color: var(--color-text); }
</style>
